  'A realistic first-year anatomy plan: regions versus systems, atlas and dissection time, spotter practice from month one, and a weekly rhythm that survives the year.',
  '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"First-year anatomy has a reputation for being the subject that breaks students. It is not the difficulty of any single concept, most of anatomy is naming and relating structures you can see and touch. It is the volume, delivered on a dissection schedule that does not slow down. This guide lays out an approach that survives the year: how to organize the material, how to use atlas and dissection time, and what a realistic week looks like."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Regions Versus Systems"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Pakistani medical colleges, anatomy is taught by regions, matching the dissection sequence: upper limb, thorax, abdomen and pelvis, head and neck, and neuroanatomy to close the year. Study by regions first. Every structure is easier to remember inside a region, because the region gives you a physical story, how the nerve travels from the root to the hand, which structures it passes and supplies, as you can trace in the "},{"type":"text","text":"brachial plexus note","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/notes/brachial-plexus/"}}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems thinking is your second pass. Once the regions are done, or before a major test, pull one system across all regions: list every arterial territory, or trace the whole sympathetic pathway. Systems reviews are how anatomy stops being a hundred isolated lists and starts being one connected map. But as a first exposure, systems study before you have dissected the regions leaves you memorizing names without a spatial home for them."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Atlas, the Dissection, and the Spotter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anatomy is a visual subject examined visually. Use all three channels."}]},{"